import json,pathlib,random
R=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
rows='''1~What is the safest July snapshot of the public examinations amendment?~Parliamentary passage is recorded, but assent and commencement need separate verification.~Introduction proves commencement.|It applies identically to every classroom test.|Higher penalties prove higher conviction rates.~Legislative stages and implementation outcomes are distinct. The reviewed source records passage on30July, not an independently checked commencement notification.
2~A proposed Supreme Court strength of37judges excluding the CJI means what total including the CJI?~38~37|34|41~Adding the single CJI position gives38. A replacement Bill should not be counted as another four posts in addition to the May Ordinance increase.
3~What best distinguishes TReDS discounting from a subsidy?~It finances accepted receivables rather than automatically forgiving the borrower’s debt.~It is an unconditional fiscal grant.|It cancels every disputed invoice.|It replaces all buyer verification.~Invoice acceptance, financier participation and financing cost matter; platform registration alone does not prove prompt payment.
6~Which statement correctly describes the July rural-employment payment rules?~DBT to bank/post-office accounts is the norm, with a Union exemption by order possible in extraordinary circumstances.~Cash must always be paid without an order.|Unemployment allowance is necessarily paid entirely by the Union.|A generated payment order guarantees successful credit.~The Gazette allows an extraordinary exemption. Wages and unemployment allowance have distinct responsibilities and actual receipt must be checked.
7~A household has already used some employment days before transition. What is the sound principle?~Days used are accounted for when determining the remaining financial-year entitlement.~The household automatically gets a fresh full annual entitlement in addition.|Old wages are extinguished.|The180daycertificate deadline becomes a universal wage-payment grace period.~The transition preserves a balance-day approach and verified old liabilities; accounting deadlines are not a licence to delay every wage.
8~Which is not equivalent to wafer fabrication?~ATMP/OSAT packaging and testing~Manufacturing wafers in a fab|Producing semiconductor devices on wafers|Processing wafers in a fabrication facility~Packaging/testing is an important but distinct value-chain stage. Approved units are also different from commissioned commercial production.
9~Why should mobile-phone production not be equated with domestic value addition?~Domestic assembly may still use imported components and foreign-owned IP.~All assembled products are entirely imported finished goods.|Gross sales automatically measure net domestic content.|Export value never includes imported inputs.~Value-chain analysis separates assembly, component sourcing and design/IP ownership; incentives have differentiated eligibility conditions.
11~What was independently established in the reviewed July birth-registration Bill account?~Lok Sabha passage on31July, not passage by both Houses~Automatic citizenship for every registered birth|Enactment of every proposed judicial-verification clause|A general permission to avoid registration for two years~One-house passage and proposed delayed-registration procedures do not establish final enactment or citizenship status.
12~Under the draft foreign-investment framework, how is the10%threshold described?~FDI at10%or more and FPI below10%in company/LLP equity~FDI only above50%in every entity|Every foreign investment is debt|Exactly10%is always FPI~These are draft definitions. They should not be substituted for the reviewed2019baseline, especially its treatment of unlisted-company equity.
13~The proposed₹25lakh PMS ticket applies to which category in the consultation?~A proposed mutual-fund-only portfolio-management category~Every PMS without exception|The net worth of every client|All retail mutual-fund purchases~The consultation also proposes₹2croreapplicant net worth for that category. Client investment and manager net worth are different, and proposals are not final rules.
14~Which insurance-governance principle is described in the July regulatory review?~Policyholder funds cannot meet liabilities arising from the specified amalgamation.~Policyholder money is unrestricted shareholder capital.|Every merger is automatically approved.|The education fund pays every disputed claim in full.~Ring-fencing and board assessment of adverse policyholder effects are distinct from proof that any particular merger complied.
15~The Securities Markets Code Committee recommendations should be treated as what?~Scrutiny proposals on delegation, offences and appeals, not automatically enacted law~A new court judgment annulling all SEBI orders|Proof all exchanges have unlimited regulatory power|Automatic suspension of every SEBI order~Committee scrutiny can inform legislation. Clear delegation boundaries and independent appeals must be distinguished from final statutory text.
16~Which qualification matters when applying the reviewed waterfront policy to Andhra Pradesh?~Identify whether the port is a Union major port before applying that framework.~Every AP port is administered exclusively by the Union.|Renewal without tender always means zero price.|The policy transfers permanent land ownership to every company.~Major and non-major ports have different governance. Reviewed renewal pricing uses market/existing-revenue safeguards, not free unconditional transfer.
19~What exact PM-KISAN continuation outlay does the inspected primary release specify?~₹3.15lakhcrore~₹3.2lakhcroreexactly|₹6,000crore|₹36,441crore~The Cabinet release gives₹3.15lakhcrore for FY2026–27toFY2030–31. PRS rounds it. The annual eligible-family benefit remains₹6,000in three instalments.
21~Which is the most defensible digital-PDS evaluation?~Check eligible inclusion, failed authentication and actual food receipt alongside database coverage.~Every deleted card proves fraud.|Aadhaar seeding guarantees nutrition adequacy.|A committee report automatically replaces food with cash nationwide.~Digitisation and entitlement fulfilment are different. Administrative deletions and authentication need verification and accessible correction mechanisms.
22~When is distribution under the reviewed revised broken-rice norms scheduled to begin?~Kharif marketing season2027–28~All July2026deliveries immediately|The first day of calendar2025|Only after2047~Raw-rice broken content moves25%to10%and parboiled16%to5%. These are quality norms, not reductions in household ration kilograms.
23~Which correctly captures the29July retrospective-EC conclusions?~The2017limited notification was upheld; the2021perpetual OM was quashed prospectively.~Every existing EC automatically became void.|Every future project can start without prior EC.|All pending applications must automatically receive EC.~The Court preserved existing ECs subject to individual challenge and barred fresh applications under the impugned instruments. Prior clearance remains the norm and pending cases require specific directions.
24~A5,000MWpower scale with two-hour storage corresponds to what energy amount?~10,000MWh~2,500MWh|5,000MWperhour|10,000MWofannualelectricity~Power multiplied by duration gives energy. The scheme’s roughly700MWbaseline refers to floating PV, not all Indian solar capacity.
25~What is not established merely by offshore exploration approval?~That an expected resource addition is already commercially produced oil~Support for seismic information|A policy framework for exploration|The possibility of unsuccessful wells~Exploration estimates, discoveries, recoverable reserves and production are different stages. Cabinet approval is not a realised state-specific discovery.
31~What is the correct period for the combined₹36,441crore Khelo India/ANSF approval?~FY2026–27toFY2030–31~FY2026–27toFY2023–31|Only calendar2026|FY2035–36toFY2040–41~The primary PIB release corrects the PRS end-year typo. Funding approval and athlete-development targets are not completed outcomes or awarded Olympic hosting rights.
33~Which is the sound constitutional approach to internet restrictions?~Test legal authority, necessity, proportionality, scope, duration and less restrictive alternatives.~Any protest is by itself sufficient ground.|Indefinite shutdowns are automatically permissible.|Publication of reasons is never relevant.~Internet use engages speech and profession rights. A statutory public-order response must satisfy lawful predicates and procedural safeguards.
36~Which distinction is correct for vital statistics?~CRS continuously registers events; SRS supplies sample-based demographic estimates.~CRS is only a five-year opinion poll.|Every registered death necessarily has a medical cause certificate.|The2024report measures only July2026births.~Completeness, timeliness and cause-of-death certification measure different qualities. An estimated denominator also affects completeness ratios.
44~White Rabbit timing should not be confused with which claim?~That India changed its time zone or achieved universally invulnerable timing~Precision time transfer over fibre|Traceability to a maintained time standard|Timing needs in financial and telecom systems~IST remains UTC+5:30. Demonstration, national rollout and security assurance are separate issues; redundancy and calibration remain important.
48~Which quantum-computing statement is scientifically sound?~Superposition does not allow simply reading every possible answer, and logical reliability differs from raw qubit count.~Entanglement sends usable messages faster than light.|Every quantum computer is faster on every task.|All qubit platforms use identical temperatures.~Algorithm design, measurement, noise and error-correction overhead constrain useful capability. Avoid marketing claims based solely on physical-qubit totals.
52~Which treatment of the Hero investment report is sound?~Separate the₹750croreparts centre from the wider₹3,200croreexpansion announcement and verify overlap.~Both sums prove completed July expenditure.|Projected jobs are already verified permanent employment.|The site must be the well-known Madanapalle town.~The report locates this Madanapalle in Satyavedu mandal,Tirupati. Foundation, expansion intent, commercial operation and realised jobs are distinct.
53~The reported Union Bank SHG decision in AP is best described as what?~A processing/inspection fee waiver, not principal or all-interest cancellation~Cancellation of every woman’s debt at every bank|A universal interest-free loan statute|A waiver applying only to corporate bonds~The Telugu report concerns specified SHG charges. The original bank circular and headline savings assumptions were not independently reconciled.
54~What caution is necessary about the412tribal Aadhaar centres report?~The headline says cancellation, while quoted officials describe temporary suspension pending correction.~Every beneficiary’s Aadhaar was permanently cancelled.|All allegations were finally proved in court.|Aadhaar conclusively establishes citizenship.~Original UIDAI orders were not read. Agency compliance action must be distinguished from resident identity validity and legal guilt.
57~Which accurately describes the reported NiVU rollout?~A phased three-year Explurger partnership, with30sites in the first year and over100planned~A completed rollout at every AP destination|A mandatory downloaded app for every visitor|Proof every generated historical answer is correct~The report describes QR-based voice/text access and Mangalagiri pilots. A target is not completion and AI output needs curation and privacy safeguards.
59~AP’s5.39%headline CPI and8.18%food inflation in the13July release refer to which period?~June2026year-on-year, provisional~July2026month-on-month, final|An annual GDP growth rate|The CPI index level itself~The primary release uses2024=100. Publication month, reference month, rate and index level must remain distinct.
65~What is the correct interpretation of the15%skill-guarantee figure?~An aggregate relevant-year claim payout cap, not individual default cover~The only guarantee percentage for every borrower|An automatic borrower interest subsidy|A promise that15%of every course fee is a grant~PRS describes individual cover75%up to₹4lakh and70%above₹4lakh to₹7.5lakh. Portfolio ceiling, individual guarantee and borrower repayment are different.'''
Q=[]
for i,line in enumerate(rows.splitlines(),1):
 ref,question,correct,other,why=line.split('~');opts=[correct]+other.split('|');random.Random(1400+i).shuffle(opts)
 Q.append(dict(id=f'JUL26-{i:02}',question=question,options=opts,answer=opts.index(correct),explanation=why,ref=f'E14-2607-{int(ref):03}'))
assert len(Q)==30
# Deliberate, bounded typography: separate tokens in question prose, not IDs/URLs.
import re
for q in Q:
 for k in ['question','explanation']:
  q[k]=re.sub(r'(?<=[a-zA-Z])(?=[0-9₹])|(?<=[0-9])(?=[a-zA-Z₹])',' ',q[k])
 q['options']=[re.sub(r'(?<=[a-zA-Z])(?=[0-9₹])|(?<=[0-9])(?=[a-zA-Z₹])',' ',o) for o in q['options']]
(R/'data/2026-07-mcqs.json').write_text(json.dumps(Q,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
F=[
(1,'Examination integrity requires more than higher punishments.', ['Anchor parliamentary passage on30July, separately checking assent/commencement before asserting operative law.','Map secure question production, delivery, centre management, vendor contracts and evidence preservation.','Balance investigative capacity and faster trials with competent counsel, judicial independence and reliable digital forensics.','For APPSC, distinguish central statutory scope from the state recruitment framework and avoid assuming identical jurisdiction.','Measure leak incidence, timely reasoned disposal, candidate redress and vendor accountability rather than only maximum penalties.']),
(7,'A rural-employment transition must preserve both rights and records.', ['Anchor1July payment and transitional rules; old liabilities are verified up to30June.','Explain carry-forward works/cards, used-days adjustment, assets and auditable liability reconciliation.','Distinguish wages, unemployment allowance, household entitlement and accounting-certificate deadlines.','For AP, propose assisted eKYC/payment correction, work-demand receipts and village-level publication of used/balance days.','Use social audit to link records, actual worker receipts and physical assets without publishing excessive personal data.']),
(8,'Technological sovereignty depends on value-chain capability, not factory announcements.', ['Anchor15July Semicon2.0 and mobile-manufacturing approvals, separating approved outlay from expenditure.','Map design/IP, equipment/materials, fabs, packaging/testing, R&D and talent as complementary stages.','Compare gross assembly/export values with domestic content, productivity and commercial sustainability.','Discuss subsidy cost, water/power demand, environmental compliance, trusted partnerships and local supplier learning.','For AP, propose skill/supplier linkages without inventing a new fab approval; evaluate incremental capability rather than announcement counts.']),
(23,'Environmental regularisation must not become a substitute for prior clearance.', ['Anchor29July judgment: limited2017notification upheld, perpetual2021OMquashed prospectively.','Explain legal hierarchy: administrative instruction cannot supplant delegated legislation; prior EC remains normative.','Preserve existing ECs subject to individual challenge, specific treatment of pending cases and bar on fresh applications under the impugned instruments.','Discuss moral hazard, public interest, legal certainty and the limits of administrative amnesties; do not claim every pending project is cleared.','For AP infrastructure, recommend project-specific compliance chronology, transparent appraisal and cumulative-impact monitoring.']),
(24,'Floating solar is a joint energy–water governance challenge.', ['Anchor31July approval,5000MWwith two-hour storage,₹5070croreoutlay and post-commissioning support.','Explain power versus energy:5000MW×2hours=10000MWh;700MWbaseline means floating PVonly.','Assess reservoir drawdown, bathymetry, anchoring, fisheries, ecological effects, dam safety and grid evacuation.','For AP, identify responsible reservoir/power institutions and consult water users; no named reservoir allocation is verified.','Use feasibility, safe storage, measured commissioning and lifecycle performance rather than theoretical potential as the investment test.']),
(55,'Disability certification should respond to progressive functional loss.', ['Anchor2July reporting on BMD/Huntington cases and reassessment delays, not a complete eligibility-law audit.','Distinguish diagnosis, functional impairment assessment, certificate and pension entitlement.','Examine travel, appointment, expertise, digital payment/booking and appeal barriers for home-bound patients and caregivers.','Recommend trained multidisciplinary boards, accessible reassessment, reasoned decisions and time-bound remedies under applicable law.','Connect rights-based welfare with dignity and measurable waiting-time/appeal outcomes; avoid unsupported automatic-percentage promises.']),
(57,'AI-enabled tourism needs cultural accountability and privacy by design.', ['Anchor7July Explurger/NiVU partnership: phased30sites in yearone,over100planned in three years.','Explain potential multilingual access through QR/voice/text, while separating pilot, MoU and completed deployment.','Assess historical accuracy, local expert curation, unsafe advice, accessibility, low connectivity and hallucinations.','Limit analytics to necessary data with clear notices, secure retention and human correction; preserve non-smartphone access.','Measure answer reliability and visitor inclusion rather than first-state publicity or scan counts.']),
(59,'State inflation analysis must preserve the reference month and distributional context.', ['Anchor13July primary release forJune: APheadline5.39%,CFPI8.18%; India4.38%and5.32%,provisional.','Distinguish index levels,year-on-year rates,month-on-month changes and quarterly averages under the2024base.','Examine food supply,storage,logistics,perishability and unequal household expenditure burdens.','For AP, combine transparent market monitoring,targeted support and supply-chain measures without attributing the entire gap to one cause.','Conclude with revised data checks and equity-sensitive outcomes rather than headline inflation alone.'])]
